# Rust library crate — gitignore.
#
# `target/` is always ignored (build output).
# `Cargo.lock` IS gitignored for libraries: downstream consumers resolve
# their own deps. Committing the lockfile of a library only pins the
# *test* environment and produces noisy merge conflicts.
# For binary crates the rule is reversed; see `code/rust-binary/`.

# Build output
/target/

# Library lockfile is not committed
Cargo.lock

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
